    <a href="https://g.page/r/CQrh4y6zb339EBM/review" target="_blank">⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️ See Our Reviews</a>
  </div>

  <h2>The Anatomy of a FitFix Suit: Engineered for Excellence</h2>

  <p>What separates a truly great suit from a merely adequate one? It is the invisible architecture. At FitFix, under the masterful eye of <a href="https://fitfixclothesalterations.co.ke/about-david-ochieng/">David Ochieng</a>, we utilize traditional tailoring techniques combined with modern precision. Here is what goes into every suit we create:</p>

  <div class="prose-cols">
    <div>
      <h3>1. Full Canvas Construction</h3>
      <p>Most suits under KSh 30,000 use a "fused" construction, where a layer of glue holds the interlining to the fabric. This glue inevitably bubbles and breaks down over time, ruining the shape of the jacket. </p>
      <p>Our Signature and Executive suits feature a <strong>Full Floating Canvas</strong>. A layer of horsehair and wool canvas is placed inside the jacket and loosely stitched by hand. This allows the jacket to mold to your body over time, breathe naturally, and drape flawlessly. It is the most complex and labor-intensive way to build a suit, and it is the only way to achieve a true bespoke feel.</p>
      
      <h3>2. The Sleeve Pitch</h3>
      <p>This is the most invisible detail on a suit, but you can feel it every time you move. Sleeve pitch is the angle at which the sleeve hangs from the shoulder. Off-the-rack suits cut sleeves straight down, causing them to twist when you move. We cut and set the sleeve head by hand, ensuring it follows the natural forward curve of your arm. When you reach for a handshake or type on a keyboard, the jacket moves with you, not against you.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>3. Bemberg Cupro Lining</h3>
      <p>While the outer fabric protects you from the world, the lining protects your clothes and your comfort. We use premium Bemberg cupro lining, which is breathable, anti-static, and incredibly smooth. It allows you to slip the jacket on and off effortlessly over a <a href="https://fitfixclothesalterations.co.ke/made-to-measure/shirts/">made-to-measure shirt</a>, and prevents you from overheating in Nairobi's climate.</p>

      <h3>4. Hand-Finished Details</h3>
      <p>Look closely at a FitFix suit, and you will find details that machines simply cannot replicate. The lapels are hand-rolled (a process called *mappina*), giving them a soft, natural curve. The sleeve heads are inserted by hand to ensure they sit perfectly. The buttonholes on the jacket are hand-stitched. These are the hidden hallmarks of true bespoke tailoring.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

