  <h2>The Fabric Library: Choosing Your Armor</h2>

  <p>The fabric is the soul of the suit. It dictates how the garment feels against your skin, how it drapes on your body, and how it performs in different climates. We source our fabrics from the most prestigious mills in Italy and the UK. Here is a guide to the options available to you:</p>

  <div class="prose-cols">
    <div>
      <h3>Super 120s Wool: The Workhorse</h3>
      <p>The gold standard for business suits. Super 120s wool is lightweight, breathable, and naturally wrinkle-resistant. It holds a crease beautifully and has a subtle, matte finish that looks highly professional. It is the ideal fabric for a suit you will wear two or three times a week.</p>

      <h3>Super 150s Wool: The Executive Tier</h3>
      <p>For the ultimate luxury, we offer finer micron wool. Super 150s is incredibly soft, almost silky to the touch, yet remarkably durable. It has a superior drape that elevates the entire look of the suit. This is the fabric of choice for our <a href="https://fitfixclothesalterations.co.ke/made-to-measure/executive-mens-suits/">Executive Suit collection</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Linen and Silk Blends</h3>
      <p>Perfect for the Nairobi heat or for destination weddings. A wool-linen or wool-silk blend softens the wrinkling associated with pure linen while retaining its cool, breathable properties. It has a beautiful, textured look that is perfect for a <a href="https://fitfixclothesalterations.co.ke/groomsmen-suit-alterations/">groom's suit</a> or summer events.</p>

      <h3>Flannel and Tweed</h3>
      <p>For cooler climates or a more heritage aesthetic. Flannel is soft, brushed, and warm, while tweed offers incredible durability and texture. These are excellent choices for a winter suit or a country look.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bofu-box" style="margin:40px 0;">
