  <h2>The FitFix Process: From Measurement to Masterpiece</h2>

  <p>Creating a bespoke suit is a collaborative journey. It takes approximately 3 to 4 weeks, and we involve you at every critical stage to ensure the final result exceeds your expectations. We offer <a href="https://fitfixclothesalterations.co.ke/pickup-and-delivery/">free door-to-door pickup and delivery</a> across Nairobi to make the process as convenient as possible.</p>

  <h3>Phase 1: The Consultation & Measurement</h3>
  <p>It begins with a conversation at our Industrial Area workshop, or at your home or office. We discuss your lifestyle, your business environment, and your personal style. We then take over 30 detailed measurements, noting your posture, shoulder slope, and any asymmetries in your body. We ask how you wear your watch and which shoe you intend to wear with the suit, as these details affect the fit of the sleeve and the break of the trouser.</p>

  <h3>Phase 2: Fabric and Design Selection</h3>
  <p>We present a curated selection of fabric swatches so you can feel the weight and texture. You will choose the cloth, the lining, the button style, the lapel width, and the pocket configuration. We can even add custom monogramming to the inside jacket pocket for a truly personal touch.</p>

  <h3>Phase 3: The Basted Fitting</h3>
  <p>About two weeks after the consultation, you will try on a "basted" version of your suit. This is a rough assembly of the canvas and fabric held together by temporary white stitching. This fitting is crucial. It allows us to adjust the balance of the jacket, the position of the pockets, and the drape of the canvas on your actual body before the final sewing begins. This is where the true bespoke magic happens.</p>

  <h3>Phase 4: Final Craftsmanship and Delivery</h3>
  <p>After the basted fitting, we refine the suit and perform a final check. The lining is sewn in, the buttonholes are hand-stitched, and the suit is pressed to perfection. When it is ready, we deliver it to your door on a premium hanger and in a breathable garment bag. If any minor tweaks are required, we handle them immediately under our <a href="https://fitfixclothesalterations.co.ke/warranty/">lifetime workmanship warranty</a>.</p>

