  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>Why choose a made-to-measure suit over off-the-rack?</summary>
    <p>Off-the-rack suits are cut for a hypothetical average body. A made-to-measure suit is drafted to your specific measurements, accommodating your unique shoulder slope, posture, and drop. The result is a garment that looks and feels significantly better.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How long does it take to make a bespoke suit in Nairobi?</summary>
    <p>Standard turnaround for a made-to-measure suit is 3 to 4 weeks. This allows time for the initial consultation, basted fitting, and final adjustments. Express services are available upon request.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What is full canvas construction?</summary>
    <p>Full canvas means the suit jacket has a layer of horsehair and wool canvas running from the shoulders to the hem, loosely stitched inside by hand. This allows the jacket to mold to your body over time, providing superior drape, breathability, and longevity.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
